   "en": {
    "headline": "A developer drops Claude Code for Pi, criticising its feature bloat and instability",
    "summary_short": "A developer explains why they are switching from Claude Code to Pi, a minimalist open-source coding agent harness. The post has sparked a wide debate on Hacker News.",
    "summary_long": "Caleb, author of the blog caleb.software, had used Claude Code for over a year. Caleb is leaving it over an accumulation of small frustrations: it did not support AGENTS.md files until now, its VSCode integration has flaws, and Anthropic keeps adding enterprise-oriented features without caring for stability. By Caleb's count, Claude Code has had 244 releases this year, and over three quarters changed the model's internal instructions, which alters its behaviour.\n\nThe post also argues it uses too many tokens: the Bash tool description alone takes almost 3,000. In Caleb's view, the product lacks someone who says \"no\". The author acknowledges that Claude Code was a pioneer and that later tools like Pi learn from its mistakes, and highlights Pi's stability and how easy it is to extend.",
    "unconfirmed_claims": [
     "Claude Code has published 244 releases this year and over 3/4 changed the system prompt or tool descriptions.",
     "Claude Code's Bash tool description takes almost 3,000 tokens."
    ]
   },
