   "en": {
    "headline": "Goldman Sachs limits Claude Code and GitHub to its engineers, pulling them from bankers and traders",
    "summary_short": "Goldman Sachs now only lets its engineers use coding agents such as Claude Code. It is also one of the banks leading Anthropic's IPO.",
    "summary_long": "According to Bloomberg, internal guidance from October restricts Claude Code and GitHub to the bank's roughly 12,000 engineers, out of a staff of 47,000. Most traders and bankers lose access after a review of productivity and risks. They used the tools to track client flows, model positions and prepare materials. In July, chief information officer Marco Argenti was still praising the tools built by employees without technical training.\n\nA coding agent writes and runs programs with the same permissions as its user. A trader's code can end up in daily use without going through reviews or respecting the information barriers banks are required to keep. Goldman's in-house AI assistant remains available to everyone. Goldman and Morgan Stanley are leading Anthropic's IPO, expected on Nasdaq before the end of November.",
